WEBVTT

00:01.960 --> 00:04.796
WRITTEN BY HYUGA NATSU

01:32.050 --> 01:33.426
THIS STORY IS A FICTION AND ALL NAMES OF
FIGURES AND ORGANIZATIONS ARE FICTITIOUS.

01:33.510 --> 01:34.928
MOREOVER, THE STORY HAS NO RELATION
TO REAL-LIFE INCIDENTS AND EVENTS.

01:37.347 --> 01:39.182
<i>Sounds like insects chirping.</i>

01:40.475 --> 01:42.811
Maomao, you should wear the fox mask too,

01:42.894 --> 01:44.646
the one you painted earlier.

01:50.193 --> 01:53.238
<i>Red is usually used to line the eyes,</i>

01:53.321 --> 01:55.824
<i>but green? That's an odd choice.</i>

01:56.825 --> 01:58.409
Kind of looks like a tanuki.

01:58.493 --> 02:01.830
What?
You look like a cat yourself, Maomao.

02:04.332 --> 02:05.917
<i>My hair's getting in the way.</i>

02:07.710 --> 02:09.129
I'll re-tie it for you.

02:10.046 --> 02:10.964
Sit down.

02:16.219 --> 02:18.388
It looks a bit plain...

02:18.471 --> 02:20.640
with just the ribbon.

02:20.723 --> 02:22.183
I do not really mind.

02:22.267 --> 02:24.352
Then I'll lend you my hairpin,

02:24.435 --> 02:27.647
the spiderweb one! It's super cute.

02:28.857 --> 02:32.360
I actually have one. Can you use this?

02:33.236 --> 02:36.656
Ooh. That's a nice one, Maomao.

02:36.739 --> 02:39.075
It was a gift.

02:39.159 --> 02:40.118
Hey,

02:41.369 --> 02:43.496
if I asked you to give it to me,
would you?

02:48.251 --> 02:50.837
- No.
- Boo...

02:51.629 --> 02:53.464
<i>If I kept quiet, it would be fine,</i>

02:53.548 --> 02:57.594
<i>but Lord Jinshi is oddly good
at reading expressions.</i>

02:58.511 --> 03:01.306
<i>Well, before worrying about that,</i>

03:01.389 --> 03:04.559
<i>I do not even know
if I will get back to the capital.</i>

03:07.312 --> 03:09.856
- All done!
- Thanks.

03:10.523 --> 03:13.401
The festival's at the shrine
outside the village.

03:14.110 --> 03:15.904
Come on, let's go!

03:32.253 --> 03:33.755
<i>Maybe it is the torchlight,</i>

03:34.339 --> 03:36.925
<i>but they really do look like
a pack of foxes...</i>

03:41.387 --> 03:43.223
It feels like a whole different world,
doesn't it?

03:43.306 --> 03:44.140
Yeah.

03:44.724 --> 03:47.477
- Kind of weird, right?
- I suppose.

03:47.560 --> 03:51.189
<i>Though the one next to me
looks more like a green tanuki.</i>

03:52.023 --> 03:56.903
<i>Sometimes I see others with green paint
around their eyes like Shisui.</i>

03:56.986 --> 04:00.156
<i>Mostly men.
I wonder if it means something.</i>

04:03.618 --> 04:06.162
Seems like there are lots of locusts
this year.

04:06.246 --> 04:10.250
That is why they say this year's festival
has to be especially grand.

04:11.751 --> 04:14.170
<i>So it is to ward off misfortune.</i>

04:18.383 --> 04:20.426
Ground cherries do not taste good.

04:20.927 --> 04:22.220
I know.

04:22.303 --> 04:24.889
They are poisonous,
and in the pleasure district, courtesans...

04:24.973 --> 04:26.516
I know.

04:28.935 --> 04:31.312
- Disgusting.
- Sorry!

04:34.732 --> 04:37.068
When you go up here, there is the shrine.

04:37.568 --> 04:41.531
Did you know why the god worshipped here
is a fox

04:41.614 --> 04:43.783
and called the god of abundance?

04:44.367 --> 04:45.410
No.

04:45.493 --> 04:49.998
A long time ago,
a certain people lived in this region.

04:52.125 --> 04:55.420
<i>Then, a different group
came from the west.</i>

04:56.754 --> 05:00.425
<i>Most villages drove them away,</i>

05:00.508 --> 05:03.136
<i>but a few accepted them.</i>

05:04.470 --> 05:08.182
<i>The people from the west had knowledge.</i>

05:08.266 --> 05:12.687
<i>How to enrich the soil,
how to deal with pests.</i>

05:13.229 --> 05:16.316
<i>There were people in the villages
who recognized that value.</i>

05:17.608 --> 05:18.818
<i>But then</i>

05:18.901 --> 05:22.822
<i>others came to steal
the newly fertile land.</i>

05:23.990 --> 05:25.992
<i>It kept happening,</i>

05:26.075 --> 05:29.203
<i>so they eventually built
hidden settlements deep in the forest—</i>

05:30.830 --> 05:33.374
<i>to live quietly, in secret.</i>

05:40.381 --> 05:42.550
And the fox god?

05:43.134 --> 05:46.304
The foxes refer to the westerners
who brought that knowledge,

05:46.387 --> 05:48.139
they were also
the ancestors of this village.

05:49.057 --> 05:51.726
The foxes here are said to be white foxes.

05:51.809 --> 05:53.603
The masks were originally white too, right?

05:54.520 --> 05:56.064
Adding color means

05:56.147 --> 05:59.400
settling down
and blending in with the land.

06:02.820 --> 06:07.200
<i>The white fox likely symbolizes pale skin.</i>

06:07.742 --> 06:10.620
<i>Over time, it blends as bloodlines mix...</i>

06:11.204 --> 06:12.205
<i>Wait.</i>

06:13.247 --> 06:16.209
<i>I feel like I have heard this
somewhere before.</i>

06:16.292 --> 06:18.628
The men in this village,

06:18.711 --> 06:21.380
many of them cannot tell colors apart.

06:22.173 --> 06:24.467
It happens with some women too,
but not as often.

06:25.802 --> 06:27.178
<i>That explains it.</i>

06:27.261 --> 06:30.848
<i>The eye corners that are usually
painted red, are painted green instead.</i>

06:32.600 --> 06:33.935
<i>Shisui too.</i>

06:34.936 --> 06:37.230
<i>The group of Wang Mu
who came to the capital,</i>

06:37.313 --> 06:40.775
<i>and the white fox clan
that built a hidden village</i>

06:40.858 --> 06:42.360
<i>deep in the forest.</i>

06:43.694 --> 06:46.239
<i>Both came from the west</i>

06:46.322 --> 06:48.407
<i>and share the same roots.</i>

06:55.039 --> 06:58.376
You can leave your mask here, Maomao.

06:59.127 --> 07:00.795
What do they do with them?

07:00.878 --> 07:03.047
They burn them after offering them
for a year, right?

07:04.298 --> 07:06.843
Come on, this way!

07:19.313 --> 07:21.023
They even have food stalls.

07:21.107 --> 07:23.651
Yeah. Want to grab something to eat?

07:23.734 --> 07:25.069
Only if you're treating.

07:25.653 --> 07:27.613
Then how about some skewers?

07:29.031 --> 07:31.868
Frog and grasshoppers, huh...

07:31.951 --> 07:35.288
Which one do you want, Maomao?
I'll have grasshoppers!

07:35.371 --> 07:37.999
They're plump and tasty this time of year!

07:39.459 --> 07:41.419
I'll have chicken.

07:41.502 --> 07:42.336
No frog?

07:43.004 --> 07:45.506
I'd rather not see one for a while.

07:49.594 --> 07:52.430
Have you never eaten bugs before?

07:52.513 --> 07:54.974
You don't really see them sold
in the pleasure district.

07:59.687 --> 08:01.063
I told you, that's gross.

08:01.689 --> 08:04.984
Oops, my bad! There was a locust mixed in.

08:05.067 --> 08:06.694
They all look the same to me.

08:06.777 --> 08:08.821
They're totally different!

08:09.739 --> 08:12.033
This one's delicious.

08:12.658 --> 08:14.202
<i>I can't tell the difference, Shisui.</i>

08:16.621 --> 08:19.081
Hey, look in the shrine!

08:20.416 --> 08:21.584
A child?

08:21.667 --> 08:26.214
That's Kyou-u. Every year, a child
takes on the role of the god like that.

08:26.297 --> 08:27.632
Oh, really.

08:27.715 --> 08:29.717
<i>Now that I think about it,</i>

08:29.800 --> 08:32.220
<i>that brat did paint a pretty good mask.</i>

08:33.346 --> 08:36.599
Still, it's impressive
how still he can sit.

08:36.682 --> 08:40.686
They take turns throughout the night.
Everyone wants a turn.

08:41.812 --> 08:44.065
It becomes a special memory.

08:44.857 --> 08:48.653
It should be time for a switch soon.
Let's go wait behind the shrine.

08:51.447 --> 08:54.575
Hey, look at this!

08:54.659 --> 08:56.369
What the heck is this?

08:56.452 --> 08:57.495
What's wrong?

08:57.578 --> 09:01.958
Ah. This rice stalk's all hollow.
It's the one the village chief gave us.

09:02.041 --> 09:06.003
His field's got a patch
where the rice grows really badly.

09:06.087 --> 09:09.674
He's stingy,
so he only gives us stuff from there.

09:09.757 --> 09:13.135
- Cheapskate!
- Just give up this year, yeah?

09:13.928 --> 09:15.596
This one's better, isn't it?

09:16.097 --> 09:17.682
Huh, really?

09:18.891 --> 09:20.851
Yay, thanks!

09:23.604 --> 09:25.523
Maomao, you're so kind.

09:25.606 --> 09:28.568
Not really. No point in me keeping it.

09:29.193 --> 09:30.027
Hey, sis!

09:31.529 --> 09:35.283
- How'd I do?
- You did great!

09:36.951 --> 09:39.870
I wish Mom could've seen it.

09:42.415 --> 09:45.501
<i>He doesn't live with his mother?</i>

09:46.335 --> 09:50.089
Let's go watch them burn
last year's masks.

10:03.269 --> 10:05.980
Hey, what did you write for your wish?

10:06.063 --> 10:07.273
Wish?

10:07.356 --> 10:09.734
"If your mask burns up completely
and ascends to the heavens,

10:09.817 --> 10:13.279
your wish will come true."
That's what they say.

10:13.362 --> 10:15.823
- Didn't you write one?
- I just found out.

10:15.906 --> 10:19.452
I figured you wouldn't believe
in that kind of superstition.

10:19.535 --> 10:23.414
It's not a superstition! It totally works.

10:23.497 --> 10:27.460
That's why last year I drew my mask
carefully and wrote my wish on it.

10:28.044 --> 10:31.213
- What did you write?
- Like I'd tell you!

10:31.297 --> 10:33.966
- Oh, right.
- Look, here they come.

10:43.225 --> 10:46.062
Kyou-u, didn't you want to
play that role too?

10:47.021 --> 10:50.941
I'm not a kid anymore.
I let the others have a go.

10:51.025 --> 10:54.028
- Such a grown-up.
<i>- Putting on a brave face, huh.</i>

11:26.102 --> 11:29.480
- Did you find your mask, Kyou-u?
- Not sure.

11:30.940 --> 11:33.025
I hope it burns up completely.

11:48.374 --> 11:51.001
Wishes that cannot come true
sink to the bottom...

11:51.585 --> 11:53.254
and become nourishment
for future blessings.

11:55.506 --> 11:57.758
Insects cannot survive the winter.

11:57.842 --> 12:00.428
They only leave behind their young...

12:10.646 --> 12:12.231
I'm home!

12:17.653 --> 12:20.489
You're back. Had dinner?

12:20.573 --> 12:21.782
I'll eat!

12:28.080 --> 12:29.373
How was the festival?

12:30.124 --> 12:34.253
Um, well... Just as we arrived,
Kyou-u was inside the shrine...

12:34.962 --> 12:36.046
What is it?

12:37.381 --> 12:40.468
I thought it might be time for you
to fulfil your promise.

12:40.551 --> 12:42.970
You mean the medicine to revive the dead.

12:43.846 --> 12:46.724
Do you understand your position?

12:48.434 --> 12:50.519
<i>Technically, I'm a hostage,</i>

12:50.603 --> 12:53.731
<i>but there are no restraints,
and they treat me well.</i>

12:53.814 --> 12:57.693
<i>Is it that they think I won't run?
Or is there another reason.</i>

12:58.694 --> 13:01.530
<i>Their behavior just doesn't sit right.</i>

13:01.614 --> 13:04.116
<i>Still, what matters now is...</i>

13:05.201 --> 13:06.118
Fine.

13:06.202 --> 13:09.079
You used datura and pufferfish, right?
What ratio?

13:09.163 --> 13:12.708
What else did you use?
How much is the ideal dose?

13:12.791 --> 13:15.753
And what was the condition
of the revived person?

13:15.836 --> 13:18.589
How conscious were they?
Could they move right away?

13:20.007 --> 13:21.800
I do not think datura is necessary.

13:21.884 --> 13:22.718
Not necessary?

13:23.302 --> 13:25.679
It was in the foreign records,

13:25.763 --> 13:29.683
but it only prolongs unconsciousness.
Probably used to make people

13:29.767 --> 13:32.937
lose consciousness when enslaving them.

13:33.020 --> 13:34.980
That was its original use.

13:36.065 --> 13:38.192
I got off lightly,

13:38.275 --> 13:40.819
but if you fail, it causes memory loss.

13:40.903 --> 13:43.781
It still needs a lot of refinement
before being tested on humans.

13:44.365 --> 13:45.658
Feel free to use me.

13:45.741 --> 13:47.326
I will not test it on you.

13:47.409 --> 13:49.453
Why not! No need to hold back!

13:49.537 --> 13:50.704
You're a hostage.

13:52.331 --> 13:54.041
I'm glad you two get along.

13:54.875 --> 13:58.003
You don't have many friends,
do you? Either of you.

13:58.087 --> 14:00.297
- Shut up.
- Quiet.

14:04.343 --> 14:08.472
- You're close with Shisui, aren't you?
- Do I seem so?

14:09.306 --> 14:12.518
<i>I wanted to ask Shisui more.</i>

14:12.601 --> 14:14.853
<i>Why she brought me here,</i>

14:14.937 --> 14:17.481
<i>what her goals are,</i>

14:18.899 --> 14:22.111
<i>who they are...?</i>

14:30.327 --> 14:33.122
All of these... are medicinal herbs?

14:33.706 --> 14:35.875
Yes. I'm going out.

14:35.958 --> 14:39.253
There are guards outside,
so don't even think about running.

14:42.089 --> 14:44.550
I doubt she'll try.

14:44.633 --> 14:47.887
Hey, what'd you do
to need guards watching you?

14:51.807 --> 14:54.685
Maomao, breakfast's getting cold.

14:54.768 --> 14:55.811
I'll eat later.

14:57.521 --> 15:00.149
Come on, don't say that!

15:00.232 --> 15:03.777
Here, get changed. I'll help.

15:03.861 --> 15:06.447
Whoa, lazy much?

15:06.530 --> 15:09.366
Acting all high and mighty,
like Lady Shenmei.

15:10.326 --> 15:11.452
Shenmei?

15:13.329 --> 15:14.830
There we go!

15:15.706 --> 15:19.043
Kyou-u, clear the dishes.

15:22.630 --> 15:25.007
He seems like a rich kid.

15:25.883 --> 15:27.301
Even rich kids can fall.

15:27.384 --> 15:30.721
No guarantee he'll stay one forever.

15:30.804 --> 15:32.264
I suppose so.

15:33.307 --> 15:36.060
Maomao, where's the hairpin
from yesterday?

15:36.143 --> 15:37.519
By the bed.

15:37.603 --> 15:40.648
Geez, don't just leave it lying around.

15:42.191 --> 15:45.736
That's a nice one,
you shouldn't treat it so carelessly.

15:45.819 --> 15:47.321
Someone might steal it.

15:47.404 --> 15:49.073
Think it'd sell for a good price?

15:49.156 --> 15:50.991
It's not about price,

15:51.075 --> 15:54.870
it's the craftsmanship.
The patterns, the artisan's skill...

15:54.954 --> 15:59.291
Someone in the know
could probably tell who commissioned it.

15:59.375 --> 16:01.669
So I can't sell it then.

16:02.252 --> 16:06.173
<i>The one who gave it to me is clingy,
will probably come after it.</i>

16:06.674 --> 16:09.677
You'd have to melt it down for the metal.

16:09.760 --> 16:11.762
That'd be a waste.

16:13.472 --> 16:15.391
Feels like it's missing something.

16:19.979 --> 16:21.355
There, all done.

16:22.523 --> 16:24.191
You're good at this.

16:24.274 --> 16:27.319
Of course. If I was slow, I'd get hit.

16:27.903 --> 16:28.737
Hit?

16:29.321 --> 16:33.283
If I couldn't give a proper massage,
I'd get boiling water thrown on me.

16:33.367 --> 16:35.035
So I had to learn quickly.

16:35.119 --> 16:38.706
That's awful. What a terrible master.

16:39.373 --> 16:40.207
No.

16:40.916 --> 16:43.085
It was my mother.

16:46.088 --> 16:50.426
I don't want you to go through scary stuff
like that, Maomao. So behave, okay?

16:51.510 --> 16:53.345
I'm going out too today.

17:17.870 --> 17:19.872
<i>Has it been about six hours?</i>

17:24.543 --> 17:28.297
<i>Incredible.
I can see all the way beyond the village.</i>

17:31.425 --> 17:35.262
<i>That field... it hasn't been harvested yet.</i>

17:35.345 --> 17:37.389
<i>Actually, it's still green?</i>

17:37.890 --> 17:40.350
<i>Is that a rice storage next to it?</i>

17:41.143 --> 17:42.227
<i>Come to think of it...</i>

17:42.311 --> 17:46.148
His field's got a patch
where the rice grows really badly.

17:46.815 --> 17:50.569
<i>So that's the spot with poor growth?</i>

17:50.652 --> 17:52.654
<i>And it's a perfect rectangle.</i>

17:53.322 --> 17:54.198
<i>Could it be...</i>

17:54.281 --> 17:56.033
Hey!

17:58.077 --> 17:59.912
What are you doing here?

18:01.121 --> 18:05.501
Keep your voice down.

18:05.584 --> 18:07.920
- Where's my sister?
- No idea.

18:08.003 --> 18:09.088
Ow!

18:09.171 --> 18:11.965
Hey, do you know what that building is?

18:12.049 --> 18:15.928
Huh? Oh, that's
the old village chief's storehouse.

18:16.011 --> 18:20.432
They built a new one with raised floors
to keep rats out, so I don't think

18:20.516 --> 18:21.892
that one's used anymore.

18:24.812 --> 18:26.814
Can you get to it?

18:26.897 --> 18:29.358
You're being watched, aren't you?

18:30.192 --> 18:32.111
Well, it's not impossible.

18:32.194 --> 18:33.821
Really? How?

18:34.863 --> 18:37.866
Fine, I'll tell you.

18:37.950 --> 18:41.829
I use it to sneak out of my lessons,
after all!

18:42.538 --> 18:43.872
<i>Total brat...</i>

18:57.928 --> 18:59.054
What are we doing here?

18:59.138 --> 19:01.807
There's something I want to check.

19:02.391 --> 19:04.726
Maybe this patch
didn't get enough nutrients?

19:04.810 --> 19:07.312
- I don't think that's it.
- How do you know?

19:08.355 --> 19:13.026
This window's size matches the width
of the unripe rice exactly.

19:13.861 --> 19:17.072
<i>That patch has been lit up at night</i>

19:17.156 --> 19:18.782
<i>by the light leaking from the window.</i>

19:18.866 --> 19:22.161
Plants grow worse with more light?

19:22.244 --> 19:25.747
Usually, people say sunlight helps,

19:25.831 --> 19:30.169
but constant light, day and night,
can mess up their growth cycle.

19:31.712 --> 19:33.380
<i>Just like how you can force plants</i>

19:34.047 --> 19:37.467
<i>to bloom off-season
by changing their environment.</i>

19:39.011 --> 19:41.138
You said there are rats here, right?

19:41.221 --> 19:44.933
Yeah. Even with traps,
they never seem to go away.

19:45.017 --> 19:47.811
So, free specimens...

19:47.895 --> 19:51.565
<i>Suirei said the drug
still needs refinement</i>

19:51.648 --> 19:53.650
<i>before it can be tested on humans.</i>

19:54.735 --> 19:55.777
<i>Makes sense.</i>

19:55.861 --> 19:59.656
<i>They're testing it on small animals first.</i>

20:04.286 --> 20:05.871
<i>What a shady kid.</i>

20:07.706 --> 20:10.292
So what's inside?

20:10.375 --> 20:12.586
I've got a good idea.

20:22.262 --> 20:24.014
Ugh, rats.

20:24.097 --> 20:27.226
<i>As I thought,
this is where they've been experimenting.</i>

20:27.309 --> 20:30.729
<i>Ugh, I want to take all of this.</i>

20:30.812 --> 20:33.190
<i>No, now's not the time.</i>

20:33.273 --> 20:34.358
What's this?

20:36.193 --> 20:39.071
Metal tubes? There's loads of them.

20:42.741 --> 20:44.326
<i>Why are those here?</i>

20:47.704 --> 20:49.456
<i>I didn't expect this.</i>

20:50.290 --> 20:52.334
<i>This is bad.</i>

20:54.211 --> 20:56.421
<i>This looks just like
a workshop for "Feifa."</i>

20:58.966 --> 21:03.804
<i>Just like the assassins who attacked
Lord Jinshi during the hunt.</i>

21:11.186 --> 21:12.437
Oh my?

21:12.521 --> 21:15.107
I wonder why the door was unlocked?

21:15.816 --> 21:18.110
Did someone forget to close it?

21:18.193 --> 21:21.947
- There's no way.
- But it was open.

21:22.030 --> 21:23.824
Who was in charge of locking up?

21:24.449 --> 21:26.952
<i>Crap! It's Lady Shenmei...</i>

21:27.619 --> 21:29.413
How strange.

21:30.831 --> 21:33.166
Is there a problem?

21:33.250 --> 21:35.877
<i>That's... the envoy from that time.</i>

21:35.961 --> 21:39.298
No, Lord Ayla. It was nothing.

21:39.923 --> 21:41.800
Just my imagination...

21:55.188 --> 21:57.524
Looks like two filthy rats

21:57.607 --> 22:00.902
have snuck in.

22:02.029 --> 22:03.363
Shen...

22:04.531 --> 22:06.074
Lady Shenmei.

22:07.909 --> 22:08.952
<i>So this is her.</i>

22:10.871 --> 22:11.872
<i>Shenmei.</i>

